<p dir="ltr"><em>London interior design studio appointed to an exceptional Grade I listed residence within John Nash's historic Regent's Park Crown Estate development, for an international client based in Dubai.</em></p>
<p dir="ltr">London - <a href="https://oraanj-interiors.co.uk">Oraanj Interior Design</a>, a London-based interior design firm, is proud to announce its appointment to a private residence at Ulster Terrace, overlooking Regent's Park.</p>
<p dir="ltr">The property forms part of Ulster Terrace, a Grade I listed John Nash terrace originally built as part of the Regent's Park Crown Estate development.</p>
<p dir="ltr">The appointment is a significant milestone for the studio and further strengthens its work within London's prime and heritage residential sector. The private client is based in Dubai, reflecting Oraanj's growing client base of international homeowners seeking specialist <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/residential-interior-design-london/">luxury residential interior design London</a> expertise for prestigious residences.</p>
<p dir="ltr">For reasons of client privacy, the identity of the homeowner and specific apartment details will remain confidential.</p>

<h2 dir="ltr"><strong>One of London's Most Architecturally Significant Residential Settings</strong></h2>
<p dir="ltr">Ulster Terrace sits within one of London's most recognisable historic landscapes, overlooking Regent's Park. It was designed by John Nash around 1824, as part of his wider Regent's Park development.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Nos. 1–17 Ulster Terrace now carry Grade I listed status, the highest statutory listing classification in England, reserved for buildings of exceptional architectural or historic interest. That designation makes this commission a great deal more than a typical luxury residential project. It calls for a genuine understanding of architecture, heritage, and how thoughtful enhancements protect investment value, as outlined in our <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/full-guide-how-interior-design-increases-property-value-in-london/">guide on how interior design increases property value in London</a>.</p>

<h2 dir="ltr"><strong>What Grade I Listed Status Actually Means?</strong></h2>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-11202 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2-Ulster-Terrace-7.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="800" />
<p dir="ltr">England has hundreds of thousands of listed buildings, but only around 2.5% carry Grade I status, the highest tier there is.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Working within a property at this level changes the brief entirely. It's no longer just a question of making a home more beautiful, it's about executing <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/interior-architecture/">prime London interior architecture</a> to adapt a historic property for contemporary living without losing the qualities that made it exceptional in the first place. That balance is central to how Oraanj has approached the Ulster Terrace project.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>Heritage Architecture Meets Contemporary International Living</strong></h3>
<p dir="ltr">Designing for a Dubai-based client brings together British architectural heritage and contemporary international expectations of luxury. Drawing on our experience with <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/seasonal-and-vacation-home-decor-styling-your-space-for-every-occasion/">seasonal and vacation home decor styling</a>, high-net-worth homeowners want their London homes to feel as considered and comfortable as their residences anywhere else in the world — but within a Grade I listed building, every intervention has to be handled with far more care.</p>
<p dir="ltr">The design considers how the following elements sit alongside one another:</p>

<ul dir="ltr">
 	<li>historic architectural character</li>
 	<li>contemporary furniture and finishes</li>
 	<li>lighting and atmosphere</li>
 	<li>bespoke joinery</li>
 	<li>spatial planning</li>
 	<li>art and decorative elements</li>
 	<li>modern lifestyle requirements</li>
 	<li>the long-term character of the property</li>
</ul>
<p dir="ltr">The goal isn't to compete with the architecture, it's to let contemporary design sit comfortably within it, introducing bespoke touches inspired by <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/contemporary-home-decorating-ideas/">contemporary home decorating ideas</a>.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>Why Ulster Terrace Matters?</strong></h3>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-11203 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2-Ulster-Terrace-4.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="800" />
<p dir="ltr">Ulster Terrace is far more than a prestigious address. It's part of John Nash's vision for Regent's Park, one of the defining pieces of urban planning in Regency London. Its stucco façades, Ionic detailing and formal composition are part of what gives the area around Regent's Park its distinctive character.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Historic England records Ulster Terrace as having been built around 1824 by John Nash as part of the Regent's Park Crown Estate development, nearly two centuries of history that any interior designer working on the property has to design alongside, not over.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>Designing Within the Crown Estate Context</strong></h3>
<p dir="ltr">Projects within the Crown Estate can come with considerations that go well beyond a typical residential refurbishment. Previous work at Ulster Terrace has shown just how much sensitivity is required here, including restrictions around architectural alterations, glazing, lighting and building services.</p>
<p dir="ltr">For Oraanj, that reinforces an approach built on careful planning rather than unnecessary intervention, carefully evaluating layout choices such as <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/open-plan-or-separate-rooms-victorian-terrace/">open plan or separate rooms in Victorian terrace</a> and period properties. Luxury in a historic residence isn't measured by how dramatically the building has been changed, often, the most successful outcome is an interior that feels like it was always meant to be there.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>A Significant Appointment for Oraanj Interior Design</strong></h3>
<p dir="ltr">Rachana Gupta, Founder of Oraanj Interior Design, said:</p>
<p dir="ltr">"To be appointed for a private residence within a Grade I listed John Nash terrace overlooking Regent's Park is an incredibly exciting moment for Oraanj. This is the kind of project where interior design has to go far beyond aesthetics, we're working within a piece of London's architectural history, so every decision has to respect that history while also creating a beautiful, highly functional home for a contemporary international client. Having led major transformations across prime postcodes including <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/interior-designer-mayfair/">Mayfair luxury residential refurbishment</a> schemes, our team is genuinely proud to see overseas clients trusting Oraanj with residences of this calibre in London."</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>A Different Kind of Luxury</strong></h3>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-11205 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2-Ulster-Terrace-1.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="800" />
<p dir="ltr">Projects like Ulster Terrace point to a broader shift in luxury residential design. Increasingly, luxury has less to do with excess and more to do with provenance, craftsmanship, architecture and individuality.</p>
<p dir="ltr">A bespoke piece of furniture built around a historic room can carry more value than an expensive statement piece bought off the shelf. A well-judged lighting scheme can bring out original architectural proportions instead of overpowering them. And thoughtful spatial planning can change how a historic building feels to live in—similar to principles on <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/how-to-make-a-narrow-london-living-room-feel-wider/">how to make a narrow London living room feel wider</a>—without touching what made it worth preserving in the first place.</p>
<p dir="ltr">That's where interior design, interior architecture and heritage sensitivity have to work together, and it's an approach that has become central to how Oraanj delivers <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/360-degree-interior-design/">complete 360-degree interior design services</a>.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>London Homes for International Clients</strong></h3>
<p dir="ltr">London continues to draw homeowners from the Middle East, Africa, Asia, Europe and further afield who keep residences in the capital. For these clients, an interior designer needs to understand not just the architecture of the property, but how a family based elsewhere actually intends to use it.</p>
<p dir="ltr">Some properties are principal homes. Others are used throughout the year for business, education, family visits or extended stays, where clients often ask <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/can-different-rooms-have-different-interior-design-styles/">can different rooms have different interior design styles</a> while maintaining an overarching design identity. Either way, it creates a particular kind of design challenge: a home that has to feel deeply personal, while also working effortlessly whenever its owners arrive in London.</p>
<p dir="ltr">The Ulster Terrace appointment reflects Oraanj's growing involvement in exactly this part of the international luxury residential market, complementing projects like our <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/knightsbridge-residence-interior-design/">Knightsbridge luxury apartment case study</a>.</p>

<h3 dir="ltr"><strong>Respecting the Past While Designing for the Future</strong></h3>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-11201 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/2-Ulster-Terrace-6.webp" alt="" width="2100" height="1366" />
<p dir="ltr">The best heritage interiors rarely try to recreate a museum. Historic buildings survive because they continue to serve a purpose. For Oraanj, the challenge at Ulster Terrace isn't preservation for its own sake, and it isn't unrestricted modernisation either, it's finding the point where heritage architecture and contemporary life sit well together, a balance also reflected in our <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/kensington-and-chelsea/">Kensington and Chelsea interior design</a> commissions.</p>
<p dir="ltr">With its Grade I designation, John Nash architecture, Regent's Park setting and connection to the historic Crown Estate, Ulster Terrace offers exactly that kind of opportunity. For Oraanj, it's both a significant achievement and a privilege, a chance to help shape the next chapter of one of London's exceptional historic residential settings.</p>


